[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:21. Mad or Not]
[00:00.440]Passage 21|文章二十一
[00:02.550]Mad or not|疯了没有？
[00:05.665]Aeroplanes are slowly driving me mad.|飞机正慢慢地把我逼疯。
[00:10.375]I live near an airport and passing planes can be heard night and day.|我住在机场附近，日夜都能听到飞机飞过的声音。
[00:16.765]The airport was built during the war,|这座机场是在战争期间修建的，
[00:20.135]but for some reason it could not be used then.|但由于某种原因，当时未能投入使用。
[00:24.000]Last year, however, it came into use.|然而，去年它投入使用了。
[00:27.925]Over a hundred people must have been driven away from their homes by the noise.|一百多人肯定是被这噪音逼得离开了家园。
[00:33.685]I am one of the few people left.|我是少数几个留下的人之一。
[00:36.920]Sometimes I think this house will be knocked down by a passing plane.|有时我想，这房子会不会被一架飞过的飞机撞倒。
[00:42.950]I have been offered a large sum of money to go away,|有人给了我一大笔钱让我离开，
[00:46.725]but I am determined to stay here.|但我决心留在这里。
[00:49.885]Everybody says I must be mad.|每个人都说我一定是疯了。
[00:53.585]And they are probably right.|他们大概是对的。